# stream.soul.game (#4159): a world's live stream for the CDN. The page reads its stream here when the cutover binding
# names this origin (`v2StreamOrigin`, tools/world-launcher/cutover.mjs; apps/web stream-cdn.ts), so viewers' reads end
# at Cloudflare's nearest edge and only its misses reach this host. Installed as /etc/caddy/sites/stream-soul-game.caddy,
# beside soul-game.caddy; the record is proxied and one cache rule makes `stream.soul.game` eligible for cache, respecting
# the origin's headers (docs/operations/cdn.md, "The stream hostname").
#
# - /s/* goes to the viewers' origin (7320) exactly as soul.game's /s/* does: the same files and the same answers. The
#   origin's Cache-Control decides what an edge keeps: a part, a baseline or a bundle header for a year (immutable), the
#   pointer for one second, a 404 or a query string never (no-store).
# - Every answer allows any page to read it (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, no credentials): the stream is public,
#   and one header for everyone keeps one cached copy for everyone. A preflight (a Range read on a baseline, from a
#   browser that does not count `bytes=0-15` as a simple header) gets its answer here, never from the origin.
# - No answer sets a cookie. Anything outside /s/* is a 404 that no one keeps: this name serves the stream and nothing else.
https://stream.soul.game {
	header {
		Access-Control-Allow-Origin "*"
		X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow"
		-Set-Cookie
	}
	@preflight method OPTIONS
	handle @preflight {
		header Access-Control-Allow-Methods "GET, HEAD"
		header Access-Control-Allow-Headers "range"
		header Access-Control-Max-Age "86400"
		header Cache-Control "no-store"
		respond 204
	}
	handle_path /s/* {
		header X-Souls-System v2
		reverse_proxy localhost:7320 {
			header_up X-Forwarded-For {client_ip}
		}
	}
	handle {
		header Cache-Control "no-store"
		respond "not here: this name serves only /s/" 404
	}
}
